{
    "version": "0.91.4",
    "description": "Agent Command: use your hosts' agent sessions from any terminal. On Windows acmd connects to hosts, and runs no sessions of its own.",
    "homepage": "https://github.com/brettmostert/agent-command",
    "license": "MIT",
    "notes": [
        "acmd's daemon now starts at logon. To use a host's sessions:",
        "  acmd remote add <name> <host:port> --fingerprint <its fingerprint>",
        "then authorize this machine on the host."
    ],
    "architecture": {
        "64bit": {
